   "body": "Finding from `cloud/i639-sonnet` (dev-swift df095b2): this bug no longer exists, so I am not opening a PR.\n\n- #1210 removed the alternating message tint. `reader.css` has no `:where(article.message:nth-of-type(even))` rule and no `--surface-alt` any more. `ReaderSeparationWebTests` already asserts that no message has a background of its own (`alphas == [0, 0, 0]`, `altDefined == 0`).\n- The folded `table.quote-blocked` is `color-mix(var(--text) var(--blocked-tint), transparent)` (5 % light, 3 % dark, `reader.css:320`) over the page `--background`, which is the same relation as the \"odd, light\" row (ratio 1.10) of the Mac check. Every message now sits on the page background, so the \"even\" case that measured 1.00 cannot occur.\n- I did not re-measure on a device; this is from the CSS and the tests. The acceptance test (\"differs from article 2's background\") has nothing left to compare: article 2 has the page background like the others.\n\nSuggest: close as obsolete (superseded by #1210), or, if the operator wants a guard, a one-line assertion in `ReaderSeparationWebTests` that the folded quote's background differs from the article's. I released the claim.\n\n·/·r·elease\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
